# React imports

Treat `react` like any other package: import the names you use. Type-only names are type imports (`import type` or an inline `type` specifier, matching `@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-imports`).

```ts
import { type ReactNode, useState } from "react";

type Props = { children: ReactNode };
```
